# The archived directory keeps its own delta (`specs/agent-issue-loop/spec.md`, listing below) and that delta is
# merged into the shipped capability spec (the grep above). `openspec validate <archived name> --type change`
# reports "Change must have at least one delta" for the archived path — the CLI resolves the name but parses no
# archived delta — and `--changes` finds an empty open set ("No items found to validate."). Neither is a defect of
# this change; the delta's presence, its merge and the directory under archive/ are what the archive owes.
$ ls openspec/changes/archive/2026-10-25-fix-retired-loop-skill-still-shipped
